{"schema_version":"1.0.0","metadata":{"trial_id":"001-concept-revise","prompting_method_id":"hallway-section-concept-revise.v0","model_id":"claude-opus-5-5","seed":11,"server_state_id":"flat-creative-superflat.v1"},"style":{"name":"Taiga Service Corridor","rationale":"Dark spruce timber over cut deepslate, cut into hillside rock. Eight 5-block bays run along X, with dark-oak posts at x=0,5,...,40. Each post stands 1 proud at z=1 on a chiseled-deepslate plinth. It carries an upside-down spruce-stair bracket on each side and on the front, plus a blackstone-button rivet. Over each post a dark-oak beam (y=6) runs out to the section plane. Wall plane is z=0. The footing is 2 courses of deepslate bricks, then a field of 3 spruce-plank courses with stripped-spruce stiles. The frieze is a stripped-spruce log plate with an upside-down spruce-stair cornice overhanging at z=1. In each panel a 2x2 niche is carved by not placing the field. It has a polished-deepslate back at z=-1 and a deepslate-tile lintel, and open spruce trapdoors trim the flanking panel strips. Floor at y=0, from the wall outward: a polished-deepslate wall strip, then the redstone channel cut down 1 at z=2 (dust on a smooth-stone bed, with a repeater at the foot of every post facing west so the signal reads as flowing +X toward the operator's room). Next comes a top-slab spruce sill, then a deepslate-tile field crossed by polished bands on the bay lines, then a polished border at the section cut. The ceiling has spruce coffers recessed 1 above the beam soffit (5 clear to beam, 6 to coffer), lipped with open spruce trapdoors. Each bay hangs one lantern on 2 chain links at the bay centre, over the walk line. Props alternate by bay: barrel and chest of stock, or a potted fern/poppy beside a comparator shown as a redstone part. Item frames are entities, so the comparators stand in for them. Rock poché lies behind the wall and above the ceiling, and the floor slab reads as a cut band."},"palette":{"manifest":["mi